<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Our Indigenous Heritage – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Indigenous Heritage</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Researching Our History</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Comprehend descriptive texts about places or events. Reading: Summarize the main points of different types of texts.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can comprehend descriptive texts about Indigenous events in Panama (e.g., "The festival has two main events: the traditional dance and the cooking contest. It's a time for the community to come together"). Can summarize the main points of a text about Indigenous history (e.g., "Identify customs practiced at the Ngäbe-Buglé community." "Describe the beadwork used in Emberá traditional clothing." "List the types of dances performed during Guna Yala ceremonies."). Can comprehend from descriptive texts details about Indigenous arts and crafts (e.g., "The Guna people use bright colors like red, yellow, and blue in their art.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows 3-4 vivid images of Indigenous Panamanian crafts or ceremonies (e.g., Emberá basket weaving, Guna molas, Ngäbe-Buglé chaquiras). Students brainstorm adjectives to describe what they see and recall vocabulary from Lesson 1 (e.g., <i>colorful, vibrant, traditional, patterns</i>). The teacher guides a brief discussion: "What Indigenous groups do you think create these? What do these items tell us about their <b>cultures</b>?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher points to one image (e.g., Guna molas) and reads a simple descriptive sentence, modeling pronunciation and stress for multisyllabic words. For example: "The Guna people create <b>vibrant</b> <b>patterns</b> in their <b>traditional</b> <b>art</b>." The teacher emphasizes the stress on 'vibrant' and 'traditional', ensuring students hear the correct rhythm.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of key vocabulary and concepts introduced or reviewed.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'vibrant' a dull color or a bright color?" (Expected answer: A bright color.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does 'traditional art' mean it's new art or art that has a long <b>history</b>?" (Expected answer: Art that has a long history.)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 minutes)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Indigenous Heritage".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short descriptive article (approx. 150-200 words) titled "The Enduring <b>Heritage</b> of the Emberá People" from a cultural blog or simplified local magazine. The text describes Emberá customs, art (especially <b>beadwork</b>), their <b>history</b> of living near rivers, and efforts to <b>preserve</b> their <b>cultural identity</b>. It includes target grammar (present simple, past simple, adjectives, present perfect) and vocabulary (e.g., <i>Indigenous, cultures, traditions, patterns, diversity, heritage, preservation, history, customs, identity, art, knowledge, community, beadwork, vibrant, colorful, preserved, traditional, diverse, ancestral, cultural, historical, preserve, respect, celebrate, honor, sustain</i>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reads and comprehends descriptive texts about Indigenous cultures in Panama, identifying main ideas and specific details about their customs and arts.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (First Reading):</b> Students read the text silently for the first time.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What is the main topic of this article? Is it about food, or about the <b>culture</b> and <b>traditions</b> of an <b>Indigenous</b> group?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read 3-4 True/False statements about the article's general content. For example: "The Emberá people primarily live in cities." (False) "They <b>have preserved</b> their unique language." (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Matching:</b> Match two simple headings (e.g., "Emberá Art" and "Daily Life") to the correct descriptive paragraphs in the text.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 minutes)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading comprehension strategies, identifying specific information, and vocabulary in context.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading comprehension for descriptive texts, summarizing specific details. Grammar: Present simple and past simple for describing Indigenous cultures, adjectives for detailed descriptions. Vocabulary: <i>Indigenous, cultures, traditions, patterns, diversity, migration, heritage, preservation, history, customs, ancestry, community, identity, art, beadwork, vibrant, colorful, preserved, traditional, diverse, ancestral, cultural, historical, preserve, respect, celebrate, honor.</i> Pronunciation: Focus on stress in multisyllabic words like 'preservation' and 'ancestral'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Reading for Detail):</b> Students re-read the article more carefully. They then answer a series of specific comprehension questions based on the text. Examples: "What type of clothing do Emberá women often wear?" (Expect: <b>traditional</b> clothing with intricate <b>beadwork</b>). "How do the Emberá <b>preserve</b> their knowledge?" (Expect: Through oral <b>traditions</b> and passing down skills). The teacher monitors and provides support for vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Completion & Summarization):</b> Students complete sentences using information directly from the text and target vocabulary. Examples: "One important <b>custom</b> practiced by the Emberá is ______." "Their <b>beadwork</b> is known for its ______ and ______ <b>patterns</b>." "Historically, the Emberá ______ in the rainforests, and they still ______ their connection to the <b>land</b>." This helps them practice extracting and rephrasing information.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction / Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students compare their answers from the previous activities. They read their completed sentences to each other, clarifying any discrepancies and discussing their understanding. The teacher encourages them to use pragmatic expressions like: "The Emberá people's <b>customs</b> are unique and valuable to our nation," or "Groups like the Emberá <b>have lived</b> here for centuries and maintain <b>traditional</b> ways."</li>
                </ol></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(15-18 minutes)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Indigenous Heritage".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Reading and Summary Chart. Students work in small groups (3-4). Each group receives a different, short descriptive text (or a paragraph from a longer text) about another Panamanian Indigenous group (e.g., Guna Yala, Ngäbe-Buglé) focusing on their unique <b>customs</b>, <b>arts</b>, or a significant historical event. The texts will use similar vocabulary and grammatical structures. Their task is to read their assigned text and collaboratively fill out a simple graphic organizer or "Fact Chart" with bullet points under headings like "Group Name," "Key <b>Customs</b>/<b>Traditions</b>," "Notable <b>Art</b>/Crafts," and "Historical Facts." They must use at least 5-7 target vocabulary words and demonstrate comprehension of the descriptive details.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme and Scenario:</b> This activity directly connects to "Researching Our History" by requiring students to extract and synthesize information about different Indigenous groups, enriching their understanding of "Our Indigenous Heritage." It also prompts sociolinguistic discussion as they read about how communities <b>preserve</b> their <b>cultural diversity</b>.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 minutes)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist for group collaboration and summary accuracy, combined with peer review of charts.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group briefly presents (reads aloud) 2-3 key facts from their completed "Fact Chart" to the class. The teacher assesses their ability to accurately summarize information from the descriptive text using target vocabulary and intelligible pronunciation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Comprehension:</b> Accurate identification and summarization of key details from the text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., <i>Indigenous, traditions, heritage, beadwork, vibrant, preserve</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity:</b> Clear and concise presentation of information, intelligible pronunciation, especially for multisyllabic words (e.g., 'Indigenous,' 'ancestry,' 'preservation').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Active participation and contribution within the group.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a brief exit ticket with the following prompts:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most interesting new fact you learned today about an <b>Indigenous culture</b> in Panama?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"On a scale of 1-5, how confident are you now in reading a text and identifying its main points about <b>cultural heritage</b>?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-6 minutes)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and Teacher reflection, and connection to next lesson.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompts:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new <b>vocabulary</b> or grammar did you practice today that will help you better understand texts about <b>Indigenous heritage</b>?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What reading strategy (e.g., looking for main ideas, scanning for details) did you find most helpful today, and why?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson? Were students engaged with the descriptive texts about <b>Indigenous cultures</b>? Were they able to effectively identify specific details and summarize main points?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? Perhaps more explicit instruction on identifying topic sentences or a different approach to reading longer descriptive paragraphs.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Next Lesson:</b> "Great job, everyone! We've read a lot about Panama's <b>Indigenous cultures</b> today. In our next lesson, we will use all this information and vocabulary to practice *speaking* about the rich <b>heritage</b> and <b>traditions</b> of these groups, sharing what we've learned and discussing ways to <b>protect</b> and <b>sustain</b> them."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(3-5 minutes)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>